// The Odyssey, the one circuit the game ships (v0.1.50): a long lap through the sky, 30 m from
// wall to wall and 5.06 km round, drawn for everything the car does. It runs fast where the car
// wants to run, folds into tight banked loops where it wants to drift, breaks off four times
// where it has to jump, and hides three shortcuts for whoever looks for them.
//
//   the launch           out of the line, over the hop: 14 m of nothing, a tap of the jump
//   the weave            a long, fast slalom, dropping to the bottom of the lap
//   the keyhole          a tight loop out to the right and back, 440 m of drifting
//   the long left        a wide banked quarter turn, climbing
//   the leap             45 m missing on the way up: the thruster's
//   the climb            a slalom up to the top of the lap, 60 m up
//   the balcony          a loop out over the void, winding down 26 m
//   the sky bowl         a banked left onto the top straight, and the gate, 18 m wide
//   the dive             down 30 m through a fast kink
//   the rift             55 m missing at the bottom of the dive
//   the scree            a slalom, and the step, 16 m missing on the way out of it
//   the west corner      a banked left, climbing, into the esses
//   the long way round   the widest loop, out to the right and back
//   the last corner      onto the run home
//
// The shortcuts (docs/tracks.md#shortcuts). The walls are as high as they look, and nothing
// stands on top of them: a car the thruster has lifted over one has left the road, and has a
// little under two and a half seconds to find it again before it is brought back to its last
// checkpoint. The three loops leave and come back to the same line, so a car that flies straight
// on where the road turns away lands on the road coming back:
//
//   the keyhole          over the wall on the thruster, at a little over top speed: the pad
//                        before it, on the left, is the hint and the speed
//   the balcony          no wall where the road turns away, and the road coming back 26 m
//                        below: straight on through the breach, nothing pressed
//   the long way round   the longest flight, too far at top speed: on a boost or the turbo
//
// No checkpoint stands inside a loop, so a shortcut lands between the same two gates it left;
// anywhere else a flight ends past a gate it has not passed, and counts for nothing.
//
// The turn angles add up to one full turn to the left; the two lengths marked A and B were
// solved for so the loop closes. The format is described in docs/tracks.md.
(
    name: "Odyssey",
    width: 30.0,
    segments: [
        // The launch, over the hop.
        Straight(length: 240.0),
        // The weave.
        Turn(angle: -35.0, radius: 110.0, transition: 22.0, banking: 12.0),
        Turn(angle: 70.0, radius: 110.0, transition: 22.0, banking: 16.0),
        Turn(angle: -35.0, radius: 110.0, transition: 22.0, banking: 12.0),
